Countrified is now fully launched! Now we have a main objective and a third-person camera.

Changes and repairs:
// - Balance of the camera in the animations of the character moving.
// - Improved interaction system.
// - Fixed impossible to open chests.
// - Fixed the zoom and scope of the weapons fixed on the screen when changing weapons while aiming.
// - Ambient sound volume increased.
// - Fixed shots passing through walls.
// - Visual rework of the store.
// - New season of skins in the store.
// - Now you can earn steam items in the game just by playing.
// - Character's running speed reduced.
// - Part of the map that held the character close to the plant was smoothed.
// - Removed space between stones in one of the flag spawns.
// - Fixed a time when you hit a feature that keeps showing up forever
// - Portuguese translation removed (with the exception of the tutorial). This was bringing a lot of bugs into the game.
// - Fixed not being able to get out of the stairs.

Features:
// - You can now switch between first and third person.

Group system replaced by the flag system, which was worked on.
// - There is an aura in the location of the flag, which is only seen when away from the flag, revealing the position of the flag and which team dominates it.
// - Now there are two teams in the game, and the team that simultaneously dominates the two flags that we have on the map for 10 min wins.
// - When a team wins, the map is reset.
// - Players have their team's flag as their initial and default spawn.
// - When dying, players automatically revive after 15 seconds, in their bed. If there is no bed, the spawn occurs on the flag dominated by the team. If there is no flag dominated by your team, then the spawn is random around the map.
// - There is no more save system on the dedicated server. It didn't make sense for us to save progress, now that we have a "match" system.
// - You can see the name of each member of the team when you get close.
// - Players from the same team appear on the map.

This was the last update for corrections and improvements in version 1.3.20.x. The next update will be V1.4.20.0 and we will have news regarding the objective of the game.

// - Fixed water bottle not recovering thirst.
// - Fixed steps with grass sound in the houses.
// - Created an animal spawn on the farm.
// - Removed shovel from the game (now it is useless, since there are no more clay constructions).
// - Decreased font size of the spawnable item widget.
// - Fixed respawn errors.
// - Corrected when throwing a gun on the floor and picking it up, it loses its ammunition.
// - Texture changed above and below the tree log when cutting.
// - Fixed when equipping backpack the mouse disappears.
// - Fixed some bugs related to the offline game.
// - Fixed shots not hitting character properly on the dedicated server.
// - Fixed bugs of not being able to hit after changing melee weapon.
// - Now there is an effect on the camera when radiation is below 400.
// - Changed the branches of the smallest tree on the map to be filled with more leaves.
// - Height of some buildings increased (consequently the scale of some objects was adjusted).
// - Fixed language bug in the main menu.
// - Sun color changed again (we are testing a lot).

- With this update we officially left the Alpha version and entered the Beta version. I decided this because in addition to having fixed most bugs, we have implemented features that already characterize our game well.

- What I consider most important about this update is that we have a new map! Why did I decide to create another one? It turns out that this first map (Medium City) was too closed for our proposal. The objective of the game is to control regions by means of flags, something that becomes more fun on a larger and more open map.

- I would like to say that the new map is not finalized, as we were having problems with the team (which even caused the delay to update), so this new map and several upgrades in the version will be released soon. This goes against what I said earlier, that we wouldn't rush updates, but it bothers me to be without updates for so long, so I decided to release anyway.

- We are now making a style transition. As you can see, some textures in the game are completely different from others, so we are leaving everything standardized.

I hope you really like the changes, good game! 

